<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jane Austen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1775–1817</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jane Austen was an English novelist whose six major novels, including Pride and Prejudice (1813), Sense and Sensibility, Emma and Persuasion, portray the lives and marriages of the landed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentry">gentry</a> with irony and wit. Published anonymously in her lifetime, they have become some of the most widely read works in English literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jane-austen.jpg" alt="Jane Austen" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cassandra Austen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CassandraAusten-JaneAusten(c.1810)_hires.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
